WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.030
Happy Death Day 2U catapults Tree into a brand
new world where she has to contend with a

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.030
new killer and work out how to close the time
loop again.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.890
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm explaining everything you need to know

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.540
about Happy Death Day 2U including hidden
details you missed in that post-credits scene,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.129
what the ending really means, the final Baby
Face reveal, and how the finale sets up the

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:15.719
third movie in the franchise.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:17.880
OK, let's get into it.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.100
Now, the timeline for this movie is pretty
complicated and there's a bunch of subplots

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.270
we need to break down to completely understand
what's going on with the multiple dimensions

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.341
and doppelgangers that show up in the film.

00:00:28.341 --> 00:00:32.520
The sequel kicks off with Carter's roommate
Ryan stuck in a time loop as he relives the

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.870
same day after getting murdered by a masked
Baby Face killer.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.760
What we soon discover though is that Ryan
and a couple of his fellow science students

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.700
have been working on a machine that's supposed
to slow down time on a molecular level.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.769
The Sisyphus Quantum Cooling Reactor – or
SISSY as it's known for short – actually

00:00:47.769 --> 00:00:52.699
kicked off the time loop in the original movie
when the machine started up unexpectedly a

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:54.899
minute after midnight on the 18th.

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:59.149
That's the day that Tree's time loop began
in the first movie and something we also discover

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:03.309
is that whenever the machine is turned on
it causes brief power outages, which means

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:06.490
it caused the blackouts we saw in the first
film.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:10.530
Tree, Ryan and Carter resolve to close the
time loop; however, there's the immediate

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:14.100
problem of the Baby Face killer stalking Ryan
on campus.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.550
When Baby Face tries to kill Ryan for a second
time, he gets knocked out by Tree and when

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:23.320
she reveals who's under the mask they discover
it's actually another version of Ryan.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.649
When he wakes up, Ryan's double explains that
he was "trying to close the loop, but somehow

00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:30.170
[he] got knocked into a parallel timeline."

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.670
He also warns them that they're all in serious
danger and that the longer they all exist

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.799
in the same dimension the worse things will
get.

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:40.219
Ryan's doppelganger says that the butterfly
effect is at work and that the solution is

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:45.429
to kill the Ryan we know from this world,
otherwise he'll create even bigger problems.

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:50.109
Ryan number 1 gets freaked out when he realises
his doppelganger is deadly serious about killing

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:54.240
him, so he ignores everyone and tries to turn
SISSY back on to fix the problem.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.539
As the machine powers up, it generates a huge
pulse and shockwave that sends everyone flying.

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:03.500
The scene cuts to Tree waking up again in
Carter's dorm room and she discovers it's

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.789
the 18th again and she's stuck in a new time
loop.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:11.750
But this time Tree has been sent to an alternate
dimension; let's call it Earth 2.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.600
But although it's a different world, there's
still a Baby Faced killer at large on the

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.170
university campus and Tree dies for the first
time in the sequel when she accidentally runs

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.060
off the hospital roof fleeing the masked murderer.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.860
When Tree wakes up again to find it's the
18th, she realises a new time loop is in effect

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.790
and she starts working with Ryan's team to
figure out how to close it.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:35.670
Tree needs to go through the time loop each
day and memorize the different algorithms

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:40.180
that Ryan's crew are testing to fix SISSY
and that's when we get the amusing montage

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.769
of Tree deciding how she should die each day
rather than die at the hands of Baby Face.

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:49.830
After more loops, Tree and Ryan's team figure
out the algorithm they need to get SISSY working

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:54.550
again and Tree also decides she wants to go
back to her own world, more on why she made

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.130
that decision later.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:00.870
But before she leaves, Tree realises she still
wants to deal with Earth 2's Baby Face so

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.260
she goes to the hospital where, although she
manages to stop Tombs from murdering Lori,

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.400
Baby Face then shows up to reveal himself
as [Doctor] Gregory.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.879
Gregory had been setting Tombs free so Lori's
murder would cover up his affair with her.

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:18.250
Fun fact: this reveal of Gregory as Baby Face
is a reference to the original script for

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.629
the first Happy Death Day movie where Gregory
and Lori were working together as the original

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:25.569
Baby Face killers who were trying to kill
Tree.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:29.540
Back in the sequel we discover that Gregory's
wife Stephanie is also in on the murderous

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.689
plan , which was hinted at earlier when she
was having an argument about a sorority girl

00:03:33.689 --> 00:03:34.739
with her husband.

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:39.189
Stephanie shoots Lori, but there's another
twist as Gregory turns the gun on his wife,

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:42.410
shoots her and quips he wanted a divorce.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:47.010
Gregory and Tree end up in an MRI examination
room where Tree turns the tables on the wicked

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.650
doctor when she switches on the machine's
magnet and a metal wheelchair flies towards

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.689
it, pinning Gregory to the scanner.

00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:58.189
Then Tree releases the screwdriver she's holding
which the magnet yanks towards the doctor,

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.400
stabbing him [dead] in the chest.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.629
Making Gregory's wife a villain in the sequel
is also a neat little easter egg to the alternate

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:06.500
ending for Happy Death Day 1.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:10.900
In the deleted ending for the first movie
which wasn't used as it tested terribly during

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.239
test screenings, the final scene has Tree
at the hospital again recovering from her

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:19.650
injuries, but then Stephanie turns up and
she murders Tree in revenge for the affair

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.470
she was having with Gregory.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.960
As for Lori's role in the sequel, well, this
time around she survives to the end of movie

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.750
thanks to Tree saving her, which is a nice
inversion of the end of the first film where

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.310
Tree killed Lori after she discovered Lori
was the one trying to kill her.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.509
Now that Baby Face has been dealt with, it's
time for Tree to be sent back to her own world,

00:04:38.509 --> 00:04:43.490
but as SISSY powers back up, Tree shares a
final kiss with Carter from Earth 2, proving

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:47.160
perhaps that even between dimensions these
two have a real connection.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.430
Although Carter was in a relationship with
Danielle on Earth 2, the way he acts around

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.759
Tree reveals his true feelings for her.

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:58.720
So, Tree is back in her world and the credits
roll, but we also get a bonus credits scene

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:00.680
that sets up the next movie.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.960
As punishment for continuing to run SISSY
in defiance of the Dean's commands, Tree,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:09.889
Carter, Ryan, Dre and Samar have been ordered
to clean up litter on the university campus.

00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:15.460
A team of government agents then roll up out
of the blue led by a Dr Isaac Parker who asks

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.900
them to come with him and answer some questions.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.110
They're taken to a DARPA facility which, for
anyone who doesn't know, is a real-life US

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.730
Defence agency.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:28.270
DARPA has taken possession of SISSY, but they
can't figure out how to work the machine.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:32.479
Ryan explains that there are many algorithms
and they need the right one to make it work,

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:35.230
and Tree points out that she can help with
that.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:39.130
Remember, she did go through all those time
loops when she was on Earth 2 and memorised

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.880
the various algorithms until Ryan got SISSY
working in that dimension again.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:48.460
Dr Parker then says they'll need a test subject,
and Tree wickedly says she thinks she has

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.000
the perfect recruit.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.900
The screen cuts to a shot of Danielle waking
up in bed screaming, a clear indication that

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.700
Danielle is going to be sent into a new time
loop in the next movie.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:02.610
Both the Danielles we've met on Earth 1 and
Earth 2 are pretty terrible people.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:07.760
Earth 1 Danielle is rude, offensive and only
really cares about her status as sorority

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.760
Queen bee.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.060
"Who's gonna pledge Kappa, now that we have
a death curse?"

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.840
"We're in crisis mode Tree."

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.860
"Eew, who are these people?"

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:21.490
"Call me as soon as you're done with your
creepy comic con meeting."

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:26.460
Earth 2 Danielle was slightly nicer and less
offensive, but more of a fake, and still very

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.940
pretentious and self-absorbed, and was possibly
mainly going out with Carter so he helped

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.500
her pass one of her courses.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.310
Plus, of course Tree discovered her cheating
on Carter with Nick.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.660
Also, in this credits scene is a sneaky little
detail about Samar which opens up another

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.300
plot point to explore in Happy Death Day 3.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.061
While he's picking up litter in the credits
scene, he finds an old discarded churro on

00:06:47.061 --> 00:06:50.530
the floor and says "who throws away a perfectly
good churro?"

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:54.740
He then proceeds to eat it, which is out of
character with the Samar we met at the beginning

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:55.740
of the movie.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:07:00.150
In the scene where he brought Ryan a churro
from the cafeteria, Samar accidentally dropped

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:03.639
it on the floor and then made a big point
about how the churro had gone to waste now

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:04.940
because it was covered in bacteria.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:09.190
So, why on earth is Samar more than happy
now in the credits scene to eat a churro that's

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.870
been on the floor for at least a day probably?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:16.530
The answer is that I think this isn't our
original Samar; it's a different version of

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.270
him from another dimension.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:22.380
When Tree was sent back to Earth 1 from Earth
2, it's possible that the original Samar on

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.470
Earth 1 was replaced by the Samar from Earth
2.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:30.099
Earth 2 Samar wouldn't necessarily have noticed
any difference yet, as just like on Earth

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:33.310
2, his surroundings and the other people would
be similar.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.759
Another possibility is that when Tree was
sent back to Earth 1 it caused some other

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:41.080
ripple effect in one of the other dimensions
of the multiverse, sending over a different

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.259
Samar doppelganger to Earth 1.

00:07:43.259 --> 00:07:47.300
Remember that when Ryan from Earth 2 is explaining
to Tree about the multiverse he says that

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.350
the Earth 2 version of Tree must have been
"knocked into [another] parallel dimension

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:56.240
somewhere in the multiverse" and that "in
theory the universe has six dimensions."

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:00.581
So, this stale churro-munching version of
Samar could have been knocked out of another

00:08:00.581 --> 00:08:03.150
dimension and into Tree's world.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:07.020
This leads me back to Ryan's doppelganger
who we met right at the beginning of the movie,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:11.879
and whose reasons for ending up on Earth 1
haven't been fully explained yet in the franchise.

00:08:11.879 --> 00:08:14.400
We do get a little clue as to what's going
on here though.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.069
It's just a little comment that's made when
Earth 2's SISSY is being fired up for the

00:08:18.069 --> 00:08:19.069
first time.

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:22.819
Carter is concerned about the amount of noise
the machine is making and they tell him not

00:08:22.819 --> 00:08:25.419
to worry as the machine won't blow up again.

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:29.630
Now, that's a crucial little detail that the
movie doesn't linger on and the exact timing

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:32.590
of when SISSY previously blew up isn't totally
clear.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:37.350
But it seems like the SISSY machine on Earth
2 had a major meltdown at some point before

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:41.800
or around the moment when SISSY went wrong
on Earth 1, which was at a minute past midnight

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.250
on the 18th.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.690
Did that SISSY event on Earth 2 trigger a
fault in the multiverse that sent a version

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:51.220
of Ryan from another dimension over to Earth
1 by accident?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.890
Ryan's doppelganger at the beginning of this
movie kept saying he was trying to close the

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.770
loop and that he needed to kill Ryan from
Earth 1 to stop him turning on the machine

00:08:58.770 --> 00:08:59.920
and creating more problems.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:04.590
So, did Ryan 1's machine trigger problems,
like a butterfly effect, in the rest of the

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.120
multiverse, including Earth 2?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.600
Or did Earth 2's machine fail first?

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:12.080
There's clearly some event that's happened
that hopefully the Happy Death Day filmmakers

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.330
plan to address in the next movie.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:18.380
Some other unanswered questions about Ryan
include what was that distortion that Ryan

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.280
1 hears on his phone each time he's in the
time loop?

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.330
Where was the call coming from?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.410
And what made Earth 1's SISSY turn itself
on around midnight at a time when the lab

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:28.410
was locked?

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:32.750
Did that SISSY explosion that happened on
Earth 2 ripple out into the other dimensions

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.890
or is there another SISSY in another dimension
going wrong and kicking off a chain of events

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.200
in the multiverse?

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:42.410
Whatever the answers are, it looks like Happy
Death Day 3 will entangle us even further

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:46.090
in a wider web of parallel dimensions and
alternate timelines.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:50.200
I'd love to hear any of your thoughts or theories
you've got in the comments below.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.190
Although Happy Death Day 2U is more complicated
than the original movie, I like the way that

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:58.700
the universe has expanded without the sequel
playing like a repeat of the first one.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.891
You might be a little disappointed if you're
looking for more of the horror elements from

00:10:01.891 --> 00:10:05.520
the first film, but the real star of Happy
Death Day has always been Jessica Rothe's

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.000
performance as Tree.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.330
And the sequel gives her an opportunity to
show that there's still room for the original

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.340
mean girl to grow as a character.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:16.300
Although Tree really wants to live what she
thinks is a better version of her life where

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.830
her mum's alive, she eventually comes to realise
that she needs to embrace the real version

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.420
of herself even if that includes the pain
that comes with it.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.600
Writer-director Christopher Landon has said
that the lesson and the theme of the movie

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.370
is that "even if there are things in your
life that you regret or things that have hurt

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.520
you, […] it's still your life, […] you
have to take ownership of it.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.320
And so you can't live in a fantasy version
of your life because it's not you."

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.420
On top of that, when Tree sees on the local
news that Carter, Lori and the police officer

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:46.820
have been killed at the hospital, she "refuses
to be the final girl and resets her own day

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:50.020
in order to save her friends" proving that
she's a worthy heroine.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.600
Now, I'd love to know what you think of the
sequel.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:55.350
Tap in the top right to vote and leave any
comments below.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:59.290
And if you enjoyed this video, a thumbs-up
and a share are hugely appreciated.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.760
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.810
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

